TY  - JOUR
TI  - The Association Between Gender-Diverse Compensation Committees and CEO Compensation
AU  - Bugeja, Martin
AU  - Matolcsy, Zoltan
AU  - Spiropoulos, Helen
AB  - We examine the association between genderdiverse compensation committees and CEO pay and find that CEO compensation levels are negatively associated with gender-diversity of the compensation committee, but not gender-diversity of the board. Furthermore, we find that excess CEO compensation is negatively related to subsequent return on assets for firms with an all-male compensation committee but not for firms with a gender-diverse compensation committee. These results suggest that CEOs do receive some level of excess compensation which can be mitigated by having one or more females on the compensation committee.
